  message: "ON THE ARC as T10, owner directive 2026-09-11 (\"add WI-jozap to the arc\"). Appended after T9 per the standing \"behind the arc = append to the arc\" rule; entry is in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/arc_finishing_order_09062026.md.\n\nRecorded there and not repeated here: the 67/166-edge self-noise measurement, the Kernel-auto-import half that survives pinning the ordering, the whole-tree sweep finding this is the ONLY unguarded next(iter(<set>)) in the tree, and the direction note (a Kernel auto-import probably deserves NO module-keyed edge rather than a deterministic wrong one; fixing that likely fixes the ordering for free, but not the reverse).\n\nSEQUENCING, flagged on the arc rather than acted on: T0c measures over the DRAINED SET, which includes both elixir cells, so T0c's arms run through this defect. The workaround is sufficient -- PYTHONHASHSEED=0 on every arm, with each arm verified to reproduce ITSELF before being diffed, which is what #908 and #910 did -- so T10 does not block T0c; it makes T0c's elixir arms depend on remembering the seed. Moving it earlier is the owner's call."  # c28f
